TEXT 920 -456 Left 2 ;NOTE: Calculation and simulation of iron lost!\nGiven e.g. the iron resistance rfe=444k\nSet soft=1 and psi_0=0\nSet rfe*1*fact1 to the middle leg (set as reference leg)\nAccording to the magnetic resistance of the other legs\nset rfe=0.5*fact1 to the right leg (area=area/2) Rm=2*Rm middle leg\nand rfe=0.25*fact1 to the left leg (area=area/2,length=length*2) Rm=4*Rm middle leg\nNow simulate first with fact1=1 and get the active powerlost at the power meter\nYou know that the power should be about 120kW for the whole circuit (Pfe=U*U/Rfe=230k*230k/444.4k=120kW)\nSet now fact1 to a value where powerlost is 120KW after simulation done.
