TEXT 296 -48 Left 5 ;Lower left and right limb
TEXT 920 -336 Left 2 ;Constructing the 9limb transformer:\nGuess the length and area of all the legs\nSet the middle legs as the reference leg\nlength=2.65 area=2*0.8096*0.91m2\nSet the BN and HN parameters according\nto the magnetizing shape nominal point\nIn this case HIB-core material \nBN=2.55T HN=80.7A (all values are peak values)\nSet a (0-1) and m(5,7,9,11) to get whole desired magnetizing shape\n(Lower a is more nonlinear shape)\n(Higher m is more higher endvalue of the \nmagnetic flux value)\nInitially set a=0.75 and m=9\nAt startup set Rfe to a high value e.g. 1e8\nSet the left three phase voltage source \nto a voltage of 400kV.\nInitially set Nr.of windings N=1000 \nset soft=1 psi_0=0 (soft swingin of voltage, \nno remanent flux)\nSimulate once\nRight click on leg symbols and open schematic\nand see the B-values of all leg,limbs\n1.7T Higher,Lower left and right limbs\n1.3T Middle legs\n1.1T for outher legs\nNow tune to N=640 to get the maximal B to about 2.55-3.00T \n2.9T for higher,lower left and right limbs\n2.3T for middle legs\n1.9T for outher legs\nNow for fine-tuning N test the primary currents of Pin U now for \na) soft=0 psi_0=0 (Steady state magnetizing current=small)\nb) soft=1 psi_0=0 (Magnetizing current for start at voltage zero=higher)\nc) soft=1 psi_0=1 (Magnetizing current for full remanent flux=highest)\nand see if output of Currents of transformer are as expected
TEXT 920 16 Left 2 ;For Plotting the B-H-shape of the legs,limbs:\nset soft=1 psi_0=0\nSet .step param m list 9 1 from comment to active\nLeft click on a leg,limb e.g X5\nChoose open schematic\nNow set x-axis to V(x5:hx)\nDont forget to change always x-axis varible when choosing another leg,limb \nNow click on Bx to see the B-H-magnetizing shape\nSet fact=1,2,3 according to the max flux for seeing the B,H magn. shape  \nFor e.g. fact=3 zoom to H = 0..500 to see the nominal point \n(intersection between blue and red line)
TEXT 920 -560 Left 2 ;PhiN=U1N/omega/N=230940*sqrt(2)/314.159/640=1.62
